`OutCode`, `OutCodeOf()`, `ClipRect()` and `ConfineRect()` in `src/base/clip.h` are in the global namespace, and take a rectangle as four ints: `ClipRect()` writes the clipped one back through four `int&`, `ConfineRect()` through two.

`base::Rect` (`src/base/rect.h`) and `base::Point` (`src/base/point.h`) now sit beside them, so:

- put all four in `namespace base` and qualify the callers (6 files outside `clip.h`);
- have `ClipRect()` take a `base::Rect` and the window size and return the clipped rectangle, with an invalid `Rect` (or `std::optional`) for "wholly outside", instead of a `bool` and four out-parameters;
- have `ConfineRect()` take a `base::Rect` and return the moved one or its `base::Point`.

Callers that clip with `OutCodeOf()` directly to carry a second rectangle along are the subject of T-98; do that one together with this or after it.

